{
 "brief": "A poll by Israel's public broadcaster Kan found that one-fifth of Israelis thought about emigrating over the past two years, according to Shehab Wire. The survey reflects growing preoccupation with departure from the country as October elections approach.\n\nThe findings underscore rising discussion of emigration within Israeli society. The timing of the poll coincides with scheduled elections set for October, a period when public concern about the country's trajectory often intensifies. Kan's research indicates that emigration has become a more prominent topic of consideration among a significant portion of the Israeli population.",
